{*
  Field help for the PayArc Hosted Fields payment processor settings form.
  CiviCRM appends this file to core's PaymentProcessor.hlp; the ids match
  "{payment processor type name}_{field name}" as rendered by
  CRM/Admin/Form/PaymentProcessor/Details.tpl.
*}
{crmScope extensionKey='org.chabadrichmond.payarcjs'}

{capture assign=payarcjsTokenHelp}
<p>{ts}In the PayArc dashboard open <strong>API</strong> and press the eye icon beside the <strong>bearer token</strong> (the "access token") to show it, then copy all of it. It is a long string of about a thousand characters, so it goes in this larger box.{/ts}</p>
<p>{ts}The bearer token is secret: it can charge and refund cards. CiviCRM keeps it on the server and never sends it to the browser. Anyone who has seen it should have it regenerated in the dashboard, and the new one entered here.{/ts}</p>
{/capture}

{capture assign=payarcjsClientIdHelp}
<p>{ts}On the same <strong>API</strong> page of the PayArc dashboard, press the eye icon beside the <strong>Client ID</strong> and copy it.{/ts}</p>
<p>{ts}The Client ID is public: it is sent to the donation page so PayArc's hosted card fields can load, and the card details go straight from the donor's browser to PayArc without touching this server. It cannot charge cards on its own. It must belong to the same PayArc account and environment (live or sandbox) as the bearer token above, or the card fields do not load. The System Status page reports a Client ID that PayArc does not recognise.{/ts}</p>
{/capture}

{capture assign=payarcjsUrlHelp}
<p>{ts}The PayArc API endpoint. Use the default:{/ts}</p>
<ul>
  <li>{ts}Live:{/ts} <code>https://api.payarc.net/v1</code></li>
  <li>{ts}Sandbox:{/ts} <code>https://testapi.payarc.net/v1</code></li>
</ul>
<p>{ts}The hosted card fields follow this host automatically (portal.payarc.net or testportal.payarc.net), so a processor pointed at the sandbox also loads the sandbox card fields. The System Status page warns when the live settings point at the sandbox or the test settings at the live host.{/ts}</p>
{/capture}

{capture assign=payarcjsTestNote}
<p>{ts}These are the credentials used in test mode (contribution page previews and the test-mode back-office form). They come from a PayArc <strong>sandbox</strong> account (testportal.payarc.net), which is separate from the live merchant account, and are used with the sandbox URL below.{/ts}</p>
{/capture}

{htxt id='PayArcHostedFields_user_name'}{$payarcjsClientIdHelp}{/htxt}
{htxt id='PayArcHostedFields_signature'}{$payarcjsTokenHelp}{/htxt}
{htxt id='PayArcHostedFields_url_site'}{$payarcjsUrlHelp}{/htxt}
{htxt id='PayArcHostedFields_test_user_name'}{$payarcjsTestNote}{$payarcjsClientIdHelp}{/htxt}
{htxt id='PayArcHostedFields_test_signature'}{$payarcjsTestNote}{$payarcjsTokenHelp}{/htxt}
{htxt id='PayArcHostedFields_test_url_site'}{$payarcjsTestNote}{$payarcjsUrlHelp}{/htxt}

{/crmScope}
